.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:16:This card is the short path. Follow the steps in order. Each step has one action, one acceptance line and one command. When the command prints what the acceptance line says, go to the next step.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:18:`references/templates/template-guide.md` is the long guide. Read it only when a section's fill note leaves you unsure what to write.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:20:## 1. OVERVIEW AND BOUNDS
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:24:Allowed writes: the packet folder and its `scratch/` folder.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:32:## 2. PICK THE LEVEL
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:44:| 1 | `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `implementation-summary.md` once implementation starts |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:45:| 2 | the Level 1 files plus `acceptance-criteria.md` |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:53:## 3. SCAFFOLD
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:63:Acceptance: the folder holds `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `scratch/`.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:68:## 4. READ BEFORE YOU WRITE
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:70:Open one rendered example at the same level under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/examples/level-<level>/`. Read `spec.md` and `tasks.md`.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:81:## 5. ONE ACTION PER SECTION
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:88:- `implementation-summary.md` states what changed and how it was checked. Write it last.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:99:## 6. THE PLAN SHAPE
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:101:A plan names its three phases, Setup, Implementation and Verification, one line each, under `## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES`. That is the plan template's phases fill note. More than three phases means the feature needs more than one packet. Stop and ask, as section 11 says.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:103:The plan points at `tasks.md` for the ordered work. The acceptance line and the verify command for each task live on the task lines there, as section 7 says.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:106:## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:116:## 7. TASK LINES
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:136:## 8. FILL EVERY TOKEN
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:142:A token in a packet whose `spec.md` says `Status: Draft` is a warning, so strict validation can pass with tokens still in the file. A token in any other status is an error. Do not use the warning as permission. Count the tokens.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:149:## 9. VALIDATE
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:154:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <packet folder> --strict --quiet
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:157:It prints one `RESULT:` line per packet; the first line is the folder you named, and that line decides. `RESULT: PASSED (errors=0 ...)` is the pass. Do not run it again to re-check a pass.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:163:When `spec.md` says `Status: Draft` and every error is a derived-metadata one, a `--strict` validate run repairs that metadata itself: it applies `repair-derived.cjs --apply` once, prints each file it rewrote and validates again. It does not run when `CI` is set or `SPECKIT_RULES` names a subset, and `SPECKIT_DRAFT_AUTO_REPAIR=0` turns it off.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:165:Acceptance: the `--quiet` command prints `RESULT: PASSED`.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:166:Verify: the last `--quiet` run printed `RESULT: PASSED`.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:170:## 10. CLOSE
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:176:- `implementation-summary.md` names the files that changed
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:177:- the section 9 `--quiet` run printed `RESULT: PASSED`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:180:Verify: the checks in sections 7 and 8 print what they say, and the section 9 run printed `RESULT: PASSED`.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:186:## 11. WHEN TO STOP AND ASK
