.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:557:## 17. AGENT CRITICAL RULES (PROGRESSIVE ENHANCEMENT)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:559:### Absolutely Required
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:561:- **NEVER create documentation from scratch** - Always copy from templates
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:562:- **ALWAYS copy from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/`** directory
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:563:- **ALWAYS copy ALL REQUIRED templates for chosen level**:
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:564:  - Level 1: spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md + implementation-summary.md
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:565:  - Level 2: Level 1 + acceptance-criteria.md
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:570:- **Use distributed governance for spec docs** — Any agent writing packet markdown must use the level templates, run `validate.sh --strict`, and route continuity refreshes through `/speckit:save`. Preserve `@deep-research` ownership of `research/research.md` and `@debug` ownership of `debug-delegation.md`.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:572:### Enforcement
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:574:- **Verify required templates exist** before claiming completion
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:576:- **Enforcement is `validate.sh --strict` plus `check-completion.sh`** - run both before claiming done
