.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:20:## 1. OVERVIEW
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:22:### Purpose
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:24:This asset provides the definitive source for which templates are required at each documentation level. Use it to ensure spec folders contain all mandatory files before claiming completion.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:26:For cross-phase campaigns, keep one template set per owning phase folder rather than trying to share one spec packet across unrelated branches. Shared-memory or multi-runtime sweeps can share research inputs, but each implementation or truth-reconciliation branch should still resolve to an explicit parent phase for template ownership.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:28:### Usage
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:31:2. Scaffold the required templates using the provided bash commands
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:32:3. Follow the step-by-step template usage guide for proper folder setup
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:34:5. When work spans multiple phases or multiple ownership branches, create or update the template set inside the owning phase folder and reference the sibling branches explicitly
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:38:## 2. TEMPLATE LOCATION
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:40:### Resolution Model
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:42:Spec folders are scaffolded through the Level contract resolver. The resolver selects the required files for the requested Level and renders the template content during `create.sh`; AI-facing instructions should talk about Level 1, Level 2, Level 3, Level 3+, and phase-parent contracts only.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:48:## 3. REQUIRED TEMPLATES BY LEVEL (Progressive Enhancement)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:51:Level 1 (Baseline):     spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md + implementation-summary.md
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:53:Level 2 (Verification): Level 1 + acceptance-criteria.md
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:62:| **1: Baseline**     | `spec.md` + `plan.md` + `tasks.md` + `implementation-summary.md` | (foundation)            | See Level 1 commands below |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:63:| **2: Verification** | Level 1 + `acceptance-criteria.md` | Closure criteria        | See Level 2 commands below |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:69:- **Required:** `spec.md` (lean, rendered from `templates/packet-types/phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl`), `description.json`, `graph-metadata.json`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:70:- **Prohibited at parent (live in children only):** `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `checklist.md`, `decision-record.md`, `implementation-summary.md`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:89:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/templates/inline-gate-renderer.sh \
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:92:  .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/addons/research.md.tmpl
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:100:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/templates/inline-gate-renderer.sh \
