.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:5:  - "template compliance contract"
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:20:## 1. OVERVIEW
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:22:### Core Principle
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:26:### Source of Truth
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:28:- **Generator:** `template-structure.js` `loadTemplateContract()` output (`runtime/cli/utils/template-structure.js`)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:31:### When to Use
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:34:- **After writing** any spec folder `.md` file — run `validate.sh --strict`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:35:- **When syncing** agent definitions after template changes — follow the Sync Protocol (§9)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:39:## 2. ENFORCEMENT
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:44:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <SPEC_FOLDER> --strict
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:51:## 3. LEVEL 1 CONTRACT
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:55:### spec.md — `# Feature Specification: [Title]`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:67:At every level the template also places a `measured-behavior` anchor (### Measured Behavior, no H2) right after `problem`. It has no H2, so it is not a required anchor; the `MEASURED_BEHAVIOR` rule warns when a `spec.md` stamped v2.4 or later leaves it missing or empty.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:69:### plan.md — `# Implementation Plan: [Title]`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:81:### tasks.md — `# Tasks: [Title]`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:92:### implementation-summary.md — `# Implementation Summary`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:105:## 4. LEVEL 2 CONTRACT
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:111:### spec.md — `# Feature Specification: [Title]`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:131:### plan.md — `# Implementation Plan: [Title]`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:143:L2 addenda (after core): `phase-deps` (## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES). The template carries no effort-estimation section and no second rollback section; deployment detail belongs in `rollback` (## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN). A packet written from an older template that still holds those two sections does not fail validation for keeping them.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:145:### tasks.md — `# Tasks: [Title]`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:156:### tasks.md checklist (Level 2 and above)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:171:### acceptance-criteria.md (`# Acceptance Criteria: [Title]`)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:179:### implementation-summary.md — `# Implementation Summary`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:192:## 5. LEVEL 3 CONTRACT
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:196:### decision-record.md — `# Decision Record: [Title]`
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:210:These sub-anchors are template-provided and allowed by the contract engine (`buildDecisionRecordContract()` lists them in `allowedAnchors`), but they are not currently enforced as required (`requiredAnchors: []`). The order shown above matches the template scaffold.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:214:## 6. LEVEL 3+ CONTRACT
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:218:### Governance Expansion (Level 3+ only)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:220:`spec-kit-docs.json` assigns Level 3+ the `governance-expansion` capability in addition to Level 3's `implementation`, `qa-verification`, and `architecture-decisions` presets. This activates Level-3+-only section gates across `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `implementation-summary.md` (anchors gated with `"3+"` in their `sectionGates` arrays) that are absent at Level 3.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:222:Other extended governance requirements (approval tracking, compliance checkpoints, extended checklists) are content-level concerns enforced by quality-audit.sh, not by structural template contracts.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:226:## 7. CONTENT MINIMUMS
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:243:## 8. PHASE FOLDER ADDENDA
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:245:Phase **children** (e.g., `specs/NNN-name/001-phase/`) inherit the base contract for their level plus phase-specific addenda. These are enforced automatically by `validate.sh` via `inferPhaseSpecAddenda()` in `template-structure.js`. No additional agent knowledge is needed for children — follow the base contract and validate after writing.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:247:Phase **parents** are NOT subject to Level 1–3+ structural contracts. When a folder qualifies as a phase parent (≥1 direct child matching `^[0-9]{3}-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$` AND ≥1 such child has `spec.md` OR `description.json`), the parent uses the lean phase-parent template at `templates/packet-types/phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl` exclusively and only requires the lean trio: `spec.md` + `description.json` + `graph-metadata.json`. Heavy docs (`plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `decision-record.md`, `implementation-summary.md`) live in the children, not at the parent. The validator's phase-parent branch in `check-files.sh`, `check-level-match.sh`, `check-template-source.sh`, and the native `ANCHORS_VALID` rule automatically skips Level-N expectations when `is_phase_parent($folder)` returns true.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:249:Phase-parent `spec.md` content discipline is a template convention, not a validated rule: the parent should avoid consolidation/merge/migration narratives. Required content is root purpose + sub-phase control file + what-needs-done. Migration history belongs in the changelog, not in the parent. Tolerant policy preserves legacy phase parents that retain heavy docs.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:253:## 8.5. DISCOVERING A LEVEL'S CONTRACT (DO NOT GUESS)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:255:Before authoring (or fixing) a spec folder to pass `validate.sh --strict`, ask the contract engine directly rather than copying `templates/examples/level_N/` (whose anchor ids and section order **differ** from what the validator enforces). Two checks are independent: **required anchors** (presence) and **header order** — a doc can have every anchor yet still fail on ordering.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:261:node template-structure.js level-contract 3
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:264:node template-structure.js contract 3 spec.md
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:267:node template-structure.js compare 3 spec.md <abs-path-to>/spec.md all
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:271:- **Two sources, both must pass.** Required anchors come from `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` (`levels.<N>.sectionGates`); required-header *order* comes from `template-structure.js` against `templates/<doc>.md.tmpl`. They are checked separately.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:275:- Put the maintained `_memory.continuity` frontmatter block in `implementation-summary.md` when that file exists; `spec.md` is the fallback host only when the implementation summary is absent. Resume reads the continuity tier from `implementation-summary.md`, so do not add stale continuity blocks to plan, tasks, or checklist files.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:280:## 9. SYNC PROTOCOL
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:282:When templates in `templates/` change:
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/template-compliance-contract.md:284:1. Run the relevant template and validation tests for the changed doc type
