.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:288:## 4. PLACEHOLDER_FILLED
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:291:**Description:** Detects unfilled template placeholders that should be replaced with actual content.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:293:### Patterns Detected
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:301:### Files Scanned
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:306:- `acceptance-criteria.md` (if exists)
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:309:### Lifecycle For Docs Stamped v2.3 Or Later
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:318:A doc with an older stamp, or none, keeps the ERROR it always had, and Draft changes nothing for it. The orchestrator reads every authored doc that is present. The shell mirror reads `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `decision-record.md`, and it adds `acceptance-criteria.md`, `implementation-summary.md` and `goal.md` only when they carry the stamp. A warning never fails `--strict`. The status word must be exactly Draft, so Planned, In Progress and Complete all count as any other value.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:320:### Excluded Paths
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:322:- `**/scratch/**` - Scratch files are never scanned
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:324:- `**/templates/**` - Template files are expected to have placeholders
