.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:791:### What Is Measured
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:795:### Where It Applies
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:802:The limit lives in `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` as `goalDurableBudget.errorChars`, which the validator and the goal command read, and which the template and this reference quote.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:804:### Binding Rows
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:806:On a phase parent the `binding` anchor lists each child's goal document. Every row's path must exist on disk. A row naming a child `goal.md` that was never authored is an error: the parent promises a directive the child cannot supply.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:808:### Examples
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:824:### How to Fix
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:830:## 13. CONFIGURATION
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:832:### Environment Variables
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:838:| `SPECKIT_STRICT`     | false   | Set to `true` to run the strict-only rules |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:843:`validate.sh` delegates to the Node validation orchestrator by default. In a linked worktree whose `dist` directories are symlinks, run it with `NODE_OPTIONS=\"--preserve-symlinks --preserve-symlinks-main\"`; `NODE_PRESERVE_SYMLINKS=1` alone does not cover the main module and the orchestrator then exits 0 with no output. The strict path is designed for fast packet checks: on 2026-10-25, `validate.sh specs/agents-md/001-terminal-proof-discipline --strict --no-recursive` took 1.35 to 1.38 s across three runs on the local harness, whole process included.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:845:### Draft Auto-Repair
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:847:A Draft packet can repair its own generated metadata instead of failing on it. When a `validate.sh --strict` run finds that every error comes from a derived-metadata rule that `repair-derived.cjs` can fix, it runs `repair-derived.cjs --folder <packet> --apply` once, prints each file it rewrote, and validates again. The repair rewrites generated metadata (`description.json`, `graph-metadata.json`), frontmatter packet pointers and the Spec Folder row, and never any other body text.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:849:It runs only when `spec.md` Status is Draft and every error is a derived-metadata one. It never runs for any other status, when any content rule fails, without `--strict`, when `SPECKIT_RULES` names a subset of rules, or when `CI` is set: a check in CI reads a committed tree and must not rewrite it. The last three keep "every error is derived" honest, since a narrowed or non-strict run never ran some content rules. `SPECKIT_DRAFT_AUTO_REPAIR=0` turns it off, as do `false` and `off`. Tools that run `validate.sh` as a child to read or audit a packet set the switch to `0`, so only a person or model running the validator directly gets the repair. A recursive run, including the one `validate.sh` starts by itself on a phase parent, validates each child as its own packet, so every Draft child whose errors are all derived gets its own repair, and each rewrite is printed. Set the switch to `0` to check a phase parent without writing. `validateFolder` called as a library never writes.
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:851:### Usage Examples
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/validation/validation-rules.md:858:**Run in strict mode (strict-only rules enabled; warnings stay advice):**
