.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:104:## 3. TYPE SAFETY POLICIES
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:106:### `unknown` Over `any`
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:108:**Policy**: Use `unknown` instead of `any` in public API surfaces. The `any` type disables type checking entirely. `unknown` forces callers to narrow the type before use.
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:110:```typescript
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:111:// CORRECT — unknown forces type narrowing
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:113:  if (typeof raw !== 'object' || raw === null) {
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:121:// INCORRECT — any disables all type checking
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:129:```typescript
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:130:// Interop with untyped third-party library (sqlite-vec native module)
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/quality-standards/overview-and-type-system.md:135:// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
