.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:80:In JavaScript `.js/.cjs`, files require `'use strict';` at the top. In
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:81:TypeScript, the `tsconfig.json` setting `"strict": true` enforces type-system
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:82:strictness at the compiler level, while ESM workspaces are strict by runtime
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:89:    "strict": true  // Enables all strict type-checking options
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:94:**What `strict: true` enables:**
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:95:- `strictNullChecks` - null/undefined handled explicitly
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:96:- `strictFunctionTypes` - stricter function parameter checking
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:97:- `strictBindCallApply` - stricter bind/call/apply checking
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:98:- `strictPropertyInitialization` - class properties must be initialized
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:99:- `noImplicitAny` - parameters and variables must have types
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:100:- `noImplicitThis` - `this` must have explicit type
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:101:- `alwaysStrict` - parses source in strict mode and emits strict markers where the selected module target requires them
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/overview-strict-and-naming.md:103:**Rule**: Do NOT add `'use strict';` to TypeScript source files. Use the module
