.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:156:TypeScript imports follow a four-group ordering with blank lines between groups:
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:158:```typescript
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:172:// 4. Type-only imports (grouped together)
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:173:import type { SearchOptions, SearchResult } from '../types.js';
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:174:import type { DatabaseConfig } from './core/config.js';
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:179:### Type-Only Imports
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:181:Use `import type` for imports used only in type positions. This ensures they are erased at compile time and do not create runtime dependencies. Group type-only imports together; do not interleave value and type imports from the same module.
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:183:```typescript
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:184:// CORRECT — type-only import (erased at compile time)
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:185:import type { EmbeddingProfile } from '../shared/types.js';
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:190:// INCORRECT — importing a type without `import type`
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:191:import { SearchResult } from '../types.js';  // Only used as a type
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:194:**Rule**: If an import is ONLY used in type annotations, parameter types, return types, or generic constraints, use `import type`.
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:196:### Re-export Syntax
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:198:```typescript
