.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:266:// JSDoc (JavaScript) — types in comments
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:269:// TSDoc (TypeScript) — types in code
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:276:## 5. MIXED JS/TS COEXISTENCE PATTERNS
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:280:### TypeScript Importing JavaScript
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:282:Use ESM imports for local modules and keep the emitted `.js` extension in the specifier. For CommonJS-only packages or modules, create a scoped `require` with `createRequire(import.meta.url)`; bare `require(...)` is a runtime `ReferenceError` in ESM even when `tsc` accepts it.
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:284:```typescript
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:295:For frequently imported JS modules, add a `.d.ts` declaration file co-located with the JS module and sharing its exact basename. A relative `declare module './legacy-config.js' { ... }` block does NOT type an untyped local sibling — it fails with `TS7016 (Could not find a declaration file for module …)`; use plain top-level declarations instead:
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:297:```typescript
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:299:export interface LegacyConfig {
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:304:export default config;
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:307:### Dynamic require() with try-catch
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:311:```typescript
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:318:  // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-var-requires
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:326:### 'use strict' Rule
.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/typescript/style-guide/formatting-imports-and-coexistence.md:328:- `.js` files: **ALWAYS** include `'use strict';` at the top
